The Postgres client and carrier (`std/net/postgres.ts`, `postgres-carrier.ts`), the DNS modules (`std/net/dns.ts`, `dns-config.ts`, `dns-message.ts`, `dns-resolver.ts`) and `std/sqlite.ts` now show only their API in the library reference. Members only their own class reads are `private`. Plumbing another class or module reaches into carries an `@internal` note naming the reader, such as the `PgBatcher` cap and `shed` the carrier uses and the resolver tables `DnsClient` drives. What the guides document stays public, including `PgConfig.minIterations`/`maxIterations` and `PgCarrier.runText`.

Every module opens with a header and a usage example, and every export and public method now says what its parameters and results mean. Several contracts are stated against the code:
- a SQLite statement stepped since its last `reset`, finished or not, refuses binds until `reset`;
- `PgCarrier` reports a refused plain query as `PG_CARRIER_ERROR` then `PG_CARRIER_FAILED`, and a refused batched query only as `PG_CARRIER_FAILED` with `PG_ERR_NONE`;
- `dnsParseReply` panics on a malformed query only after the reply passes its ID, QR, opcode and question-count checks;
- `DNS_RESOLVE_NOT_FOUND` also covers a search list whose every candidate is too long.

Old comments the code had outgrown are corrected: the header now imports `nish/sqlite`, `PgArrayWalker` documents `begin`, `serverFailures` counts timeouts, and a missing `/etc/hosts` means no entries.

Only comments and visibility keywords change: the comment-free syntax tree of all seven files is identical to the base. The dns and sqlite capability goldens and one sqlite error golden move only `std/...ts` positions.

