The HTTP/2 and HTTP/3 modules (`std/net/http2*.ts`, `hpack.ts`, `http3*.ts`, `qpack.ts`, `webtransport.ts`) now show only their API in the library reference. Members only their own class reads are `private`. Plumbing another class or module reaches into carries an `@internal` note naming the reader, such as the HPACK Huffman tables `qpack.ts` decodes with and the connection hooks `http2-tls.ts` and `webtransport.ts` drive. Members tests or the security records present to callers stay public, for example `HpackTable.nameStart` and `Http2Settings.headerTableSize`.

Every export and public method now says what its parameters and results mean. Docs found false against the code are corrected:
- the HTTP/2 per-type writers can still send a payload over the peer's SETTINGS_MAX_FRAME_SIZE, and `http2WriteHeader` checks no type's rules;
- `Http2Frame`'s errorCode, lastStreamId, increment and promisedId keep their last value between frames;
- `h3PutSettings` and `h3PutIdFrame` may have written the frame header before answering -1;
- `WT_CLOSED` no longer names fields that do not exist, and WebTransport `accept` and `close` can also answer H3_TOO_LARGE;
- every module-header example type-checks as written.

Only comments and visibility keywords change: the comment-free syntax tree of all nine files is identical to the base, and no golden moved.

Part of #1236

The certificate and token modules (`std/crypto/x509.ts`, `x509-random.ts`, `pki.ts`, `pki-roots.ts`, `rsa.ts`, `jwt.ts`) now show only their API in the library reference. The `JwtVerifier` and `JwtJson` scratch state is `private`. The `JwtKey` fields, the path-search state in `pki.ts` and the DER helpers in `x509.ts` carry an `@internal` note naming the reader. `JwtVerifier.sig`, the `JwtKey` constructor and `jwtAlgName` stay public because a bench and the tests use them.

Every export and public method now says what its parameters and results mean, including whether a returned object is new or shared with the caller and that a `Secret` passed in stays the caller's to wipe. Several docs are corrected against the code:
- `JwtVerifier.verify` spells out its full refusal order (it checks `aud` before `sub`, which the old doc had the other way round), and a missing `exp` is refused only while `requireExp` is set;
- `JwtVerifier.sig` keeps an earlier token's bytes after a refusal that comes before the signature is decoded;
- `pkiLoadRootsFor` ignores its default directories and bundles once `SSL_CERT_FILE` or `SSL_CERT_DIR` is set;
- the `jwt.ts`, `pki.ts` and `rsa.ts` header examples now define every name they use.

Only comments and visibility keywords change: the comment-free syntax tree of all six files is identical to the base, and no golden moved.

Part of #1236

`node scripts/gen-reference.mjs` now writes one Scalar page per module into `docs/reference/` from the doc comments of `std/**` and `runtime/nish.d.ts`, together with their routes in `scalar.config.json`. Each `std/` module gets a `nish/<path>` page, and each builtin module gets a `nish:<name>` page. `nish:region` and `nish:secret` are made from their `std/` source, and their pages use the specifier the compiler accepts. The globals go to `builtins.md`, `docs/LANGUAGE.md` is served as the Reference group's language page, and the header's "Language reference" link now opens that page instead of GitHub's copy.

TypeDoc 0.28.20 runs in-process and its JSON is rendered by the script itself: no markdown plugin is used. The `scripts/typedoc-nish-widths.mjs` plugin keeps each type as the source spells it, so pages show `i32` where TypeScript would erase it to `number`.

A page follows a fixed order:
- the lead;
- an import block, then the module's usage example;
- a card per function and class;
- the module prose, as info and warning callouts and bold-titled details;
- each function with its parameters and return;
- member tables for classes and interfaces;
- constants under Limits or Constants, each titled by its value.

The doc-comment convention that decides which prose becomes what is in `docs/README.md` under "The library reference".

The pages are generated and never edited by hand. `--check` writes nothing and fails on a stale, missing or extra page and on a stale route or header link. CI's lint job runs it next to `docs/check-links.mjs`. A change to `std/`, `runtime/nish.d.ts` or `docs/LANGUAGE.md` now regenerates `docs/reference/` in the same PR (CLAUDE.md).

Refs: docs/README.md#the-library-reference
Part of #1233

The core std modules (`std/cli*.ts`, `threads.ts`, `testing.ts`, `random.ts`, `math.ts`, `sort.ts`, `base64.ts`, `bytes.ts`, `text.ts`, `region.ts`, `secret.ts`, `std/compress/*` and `std/sync/*`) now show only their API in the library reference. Members only their own class reads are `private`. The CLI parse model, the flag table, the Huffman scratch and the `Deflater` stream calls that gzip and zlib drive carry an `@internal` note naming the reader. `Inflater.inflate`, `inPos`, `outPos` and `reset` are documented API, since the exported `INFLATE_*` constants describe them and a caller resuming a stream in pieces needs them.

Every export and public method now says what its parameters and results mean, and each module header has a lead sentence and a usage example. Several docs are corrected against the code:
- bytes after the last gzip member are read as another member's header: two or more without the `1f 8b` magic are `GZIP_ERR_HEADER`, while a single byte, or fewer than 10 that start with `1f 8b`, is `DEFLATE_ERR_TRUNCATED`;
- an `Inflater` allocates about 28 KB;
- `Rng` seeds are starting points on one 2^32 cycle, so `seed + k * 0x9E3779B9` is the same stream `k` steps later;
- `tanF64` returns `x` itself for any `|x| < 2^-27`, and `nearF64` fails two equal infinities;
- the `secret.ts` and `sync/ring.ts` header examples now compile.

Only comments and visibility keywords change: the comment-free syntax tree of all nineteen files is identical to the base. The goldens that record std line numbers move by position only, and the 19 reference pages are regenerated.

